WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.760
One day Robin Hood was on a road near Sherwood Forest.

2
00:00:06.761 --> 00:00:10.712
Little John and two more men walked with him.

3
00:00:10.713 --> 00:00:15.258
They were Arthur of Bland and Will Scarlet.

4
00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:18.033
"I'm hungry!" said Robin.

5
00:00:18.034 --> 00:00:21.374
"I'd like a good loaf of bread and some cheese."

6
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:30.391
"I know an inn nearby," said Arthur. "I'll buy us lunch."

7
00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:34.234
He soon returned with some bread and cheese.

8
00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:38.749
The four men sat behind a hedge and ate.

9
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.055
"That was good." Little John sighed.

10
00:00:42.056 --> 00:00:45.034
"Yes, it was," Robin agreed.

11
00:00:45.035 --> 00:00:52.181
"Let's finish our meal with some music. Sing for us, Will!"

12
00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:57.870
First, Will sang and then Arthur sang.

13
00:00:57.871 --> 00:01:01.366
"Now it's your turn, Little John," said Robin.

14
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:06.587
"I'm not much of a singer," Little John said modestly.

15
00:01:06.588 --> 00:01:10.164
"I spoil most songs when I sing."

16
00:01:10.165 --> 00:01:13.899
"Come on!" The other men coaxed him.

17
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.557
Finally Little John began a tune.

18
00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:22.325
"Stop!" said Robin suddenly.

19
00:01:22.326 --> 00:01:25.091
"Who's that man coming down the road?"

20
00:01:25.092 --> 00:01:26.751
The other men looked.

21
00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:30.155
"He's just a miller," said Little John.

22
00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:35.119
"He's harmless—there was no reason for me to stop singing."

23
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.619
All four men kept their eyes on the miller.

24
00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:45.770
The young man's clothes were covered with flour, and he carried a heavy sack over his shoulder.

25
00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:49.571
A thick staff rested on top of the sack.

26
00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:54.102
His hair and beard were blond and his cheeks were flushed.

27
00:01:54.103 --> 00:01:57.450
"He looks like a good, honest man," said Robin.

28
00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:59.611
"Let's play a trick on him.

29
00:01:59.612 --> 00:02:02.787
We'll act like thieves and pretend to rob him.

30
00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.383
Then we'll take him to the forest for a feast.

31
00:02:05.384 --> 00:02:07.503
But we won't steal his money.

32
00:02:07.504 --> 00:02:12.947
For every coin in his wallet, we'll give him 25 more."

33
00:02:12.948 --> 00:02:16.691
"That sounds like a good plan," said Arthur.

34
00:02:16.692 --> 00:02:19.535
Will's eyes twinkled merrily.

35
00:02:19.536 --> 00:02:21.857
"It sounds like fun!" he said.

36
00:02:21.858 --> 00:02:24.494
Little John was frowning slightly.

37
00:02:24.495 --> 00:02:30.943
"I'm very tired," he complained, "and my bones ache.

38
00:02:30.944 --> 00:02:34.875
I don't want to get into a fight with this fellow."

39
00:02:34.876 --> 00:02:36.927
Robin laughed at him.

40
00:02:36.928 --> 00:02:40.067
"There are four of us and he's alone.

41
00:02:40.068 --> 00:02:43.075
He has no prayer against us."

42
00:02:43.076 --> 00:02:46.081
The miller was now across the road.

43
00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:52.523
The four men jumped out and surrounded the frightened man.

44
00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:55.682
"Your sack looks heavy," said Robin.

45
00:02:55.683 --> 00:02:57.827
"Do you need help carrying it?"

46
00:02:57.828 --> 00:03:00.695
"Who are you?" growled the miller.

47
00:03:00.696 --> 00:03:05.904
His voice was deep and gruff, and he clearly didn't trust these strangers.

48
00:03:05.905 --> 00:03:08.915
"We're just four helpful men." Robin smiled.

49
00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:11.144
"Are you sure we can't help you?"

50
00:03:11.145 --> 00:03:13.503
"No thanks," said the miller.

51
00:03:13.504 --> 00:03:17.678
"My sack's not heavy. There's only flour inside."

52
00:03:17.679 --> 00:03:20.232
"I have a good nose for smelling money.

53
00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:24.607
I think your sack holds some heavy coins," said Robin.

54
00:03:24.608 --> 00:03:29.288
"I don't have any money with me. And let me warn you," said the miller.

55
00:03:29.289 --> 00:03:31.607
"You're near Robin Hood's home.

56
00:03:31.608 --> 00:03:37.734
If he hears you robbed an honest man, you'll be in trouble."

57
00:03:37.735 --> 00:03:42.440
"I'm not afraid of Robin Hood!" said Robin, trying not to laugh.

58
00:03:42.441 --> 00:03:45.344
"Arthur, empty this man's sack.

59
00:03:45.345 --> 00:03:48.443
I'm sure we'll find some money in there."

60
00:03:48.444 --> 00:03:52.441
"No, no! Don't ruin my flour!" cried the miller.

61
00:03:52.442 --> 00:03:57.577
"I'll get the money for you." He opened the sack and dug into the flour.

62
00:03:57.578 --> 00:04:02.759
Robin and his men gathered around the miller and leaned eagerly toward his sack.

63
00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.456
Suddenly the miller reached up—and threw flour in their faces.

64
00:04:08.457 --> 00:04:11.791
Arthur's mouth had been wide open.

65
00:04:11.792 --> 00:04:16.214
Now poor Arthur coughed so hard, he started choking!

66
00:04:16.215 --> 00:04:19.778
The miller threw more and more flour at them.

67
00:04:19.779 --> 00:04:24.440
Their hair and beards and clothes were as white as snow.

68
00:04:24.441 --> 00:04:29.106
Robin and his men rubbed their eyes—none of them could see!

69
00:04:29.107 --> 00:04:34.007
Then the miller grabbed his staff and started beating them.

70
00:04:34.008 --> 00:04:39.031
"Stop! Stop!" cried Robin. "I'm Robin Hood!"

71
00:04:39.032 --> 00:04:42.924
"Don't lie to me!" The miller smacked Robin again.

72
00:04:42.925 --> 00:04:45.796
"Robin Hood would never rob an honest man."

73
00:04:45.797 --> 00:04:50.344
Robin and his men kept rubbing their eyes.

74
00:04:50.345 --> 00:04:53.334
Little John and Will were now coughing too.

75
00:04:53.335 --> 00:04:58.512
The miller kept throwing flour and hitting everyone with his staff.

76
00:04:58.513 --> 00:05:00.885
Finally Robin found his horn.

77
00:05:00.886 --> 00:05:05.666
He blew three times and a group of his men appeared.

78
00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.162
One of the men grabbed the miller.

79
00:05:08.163 --> 00:05:10.065
"What should we do with him, Robin?"

80
00:05:10.066 --> 00:05:15.476
"Robin?" the miller said weakly. "You're really Robin Hood?"

81
00:05:15.477 --> 00:05:19.694
"That's right!" Robin's men said in one voice.

82
00:05:19.695 --> 00:05:24.123
"Oh no." The miller looked around in fear.

83
00:05:24.124 --> 00:05:27.218
"You put up quite a fight," said Robin.

84
00:05:27.219 --> 00:05:29.275
"We weren't going to rob you.

85
00:05:29.276 --> 00:05:32.517
In fact, we were going to give you money.

86
00:05:32.518 --> 00:05:34.187
What's your name, Miller?"

87
00:05:34.188 --> 00:05:35.516
"Midge."

88
00:05:35.517 --> 00:05:39.987
"Well, Midge," said Robin, "would you like to join our band?"

89
00:05:39.988 --> 00:05:42.314
Midge looked embarrassed.

90
00:05:42.315 --> 00:05:46.033
"Will you forgive me for attacking you?" he asked.

91
00:05:46.034 --> 00:05:49.650
"Of course," said Robin.

92
00:05:49.651 --> 00:05:52.580
"We always enjoy a good fight."

93
00:05:52.581 --> 00:05:57.922
Midge grinned. "Then I'll be happy to join you!"

